From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0480: fullscreen_mode, an exclusive display mode at the guest's size (the display's scaler fills the panel)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (S8; the cvar proposed in $WORK/scratch/S4/REPORT.md section 3). The SDK's SDL3 window
  code and the SDL3 display-mode API are used as they are
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: Native-panel 60 fps. Cvar fullscreen_mode (UI/Window, string, default "desktop" = today's borderless fullscreen
  at the desktop's size, nothing changes). "guest" = switch the display to the guest's video mode (video_mode_width x
  video_mode_height, resolved as xboxkrnl_video.cpp does) at the highest refresh rate that is a multiple of 60 Hz (120
  preferred); "WxH" or "WxH@Hz" (also "guest@Hz", "1080p") = that mode. SDL3 switches the display while the window is
  fullscreen (SDL_SetWindowFullscreenMode with a mode of SDL_GetFullscreenDisplayModes, then SDL_SetWindowFullscreen),
  so the window's client area is exactly the mode's size, the D3D12 presenter's swap chain is made at that size and
  paints that many pixels, and the GPU's display engine scales it to the panel. No exact size: the closest larger mode
  (SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode). No usable mode: the desktop mode, with the reason. One line either way:
  `[ui] fullscreen mode 1280x800@120.00 (requested guest = 1280x800)` or `[ui] fullscreen mode desktop (requested ...: why)`.
  The presenter logs `D3D12Presenter: swap chain 1280x800 for a 1280x800 surface (1:1), tearing allowed` (first 32).
  Not built before the next SDK build.
Bucket: REDO

0480-fullscreen-display-mode.patch (mcla-x86 S8)

Why. The presenter's swap chain is the size of the window's client area (D3D12Presenter::
ConnectOrReconnectPaintingToSurfaceFromUIThread: min(surface, 16384), DXGI_SCALING_NONE when they are equal). Fullscreen is
borderless at the desktop's size (WindowSDL::OpenImpl / ApplyNewFullscreen: SDL_SetWindowFullscreen(true) with the default
NULL mode), so on the 3200x2000 panel the presenter paints 6.4 MP for a 1280x800 guest (FSR 1 EASU+RCAS about 4.5 ms by
S4's estimate, bilinear 0.3-0.6 ms) and the DWM composes it. With the display switched to the guest's size the presenter
paints the guest's 1:1 and no shader pays for the up-scale.

Change.
  * include/rex/ui/flags.h, src/ui/window.cpp: the cvar (kRequiresRestart: it is read each time the window enters
    fullscreen; the `fullscreen` cvar's live toggle re-reads it).
  * src/ui/window_sdl.cpp (anonymous namespace): ParseFullscreenMode (desktop | guest[@Hz] | WxH[@Hz], the size part is
    video_mode_util::TryParseResolutionPreset, so 1280x800, 1080p, 4k work), GetGuestVideoModeSize (the same precedence as
    xboxkrnl_video.cpp: video_mode_width/height if set, else window_width/height, else `resolution`, else the cvars'
    defaults), ChooseDisplayMode (SDL_GetFullscreenDisplayModes of the window's display; exact size, else
    SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode; then the refresh: the one asked for (nearest, noted when more than 0.5 Hz off),
    or the best multiple of 60 Hz within 0.5 Hz (59.94 and 119.88 count): 120 first, else the highest, else, when the
    display has none at that size, the highest rate with a note), ApplyFullscreenMode (SDL_SetWindowFullscreenMode, NULL
    for the desktop kind or on any failure). OpenImpl calls it before SDL_SetWindowFullscreen(true) and, after
    SDL_ShowWindow (the window is hidden until then, SDL applies a pending fullscreen when it is shown), warns once if the
    window is not the mode's size. ApplyNewFullscreen calls it when entering fullscreen; leaving puts the desktop mode back.
  * src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp: one INFO line per swap chain (re)connection, the first 32 (window drags must not
    flood the log), with the swap chain's size, the surface's, and whether tearing is allowed. No behaviour change: the swap
    chain was and is made at the surface's size, DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_ALLOW_TEARING and Present(0, ALLOW_TEARING) as before.

What SDL3 does (thirdparty/sdl3 release-3.4.0-428-g8bf3b7215, read, not run):
  * Entering: SDL_UpdateFullscreenMode (SDL_video.c:1907) -> SDL_SetDisplayModeForDisplay -> WIN_SetDisplayMode
    (windows/SDL_windowsmodes.c:847, ChangeDisplaySettingsExW with CDS_FULLSCREEN), then WIN_SetWindowFullscreen puts a
    WS_POPUP window over the monitor's new bounds. It is the GDI mode change, not DXGI exclusive fullscreen: the swap chain
    stays a windowed flip-model one (DXGI_MWA_NO_ALT_ENTER still set), so ALLOW_TEARING keeps working; a swap chain that
    equals the monitor's mode, in a window that covers it, is what the DWM needs for independent flip [INFERENCE: DWM
    behaviour, not observed here]. The display modes carry the DEVMODE's whole
    refresh rate (120 -> 120/1; 119 and 59 are turned into 119.88 and 59.94).
  * Alt-tab / focus loss: SDL_OnWindowFocusLost -> SDL_ShouldMinimizeOnFocusLoss (SDL_VIDEO_MINIMIZE_ON_FOCUS_LOSS,
    default "auto": an exclusive-mode window minimizes) -> SDL_OnWindowMinimized -> SDL_UpdateFullscreenMode(LEAVE): the
    desktop mode is back. Restoring the window -> SDL_OnWindowRestored -> ENTER: the mode again. The environment variable
    SDL_VIDEO_MINIMIZE_ON_FOCUS_LOSS=0 keeps the mode on focus loss.
  * Leaving fullscreen (cvar `fullscreen` false) and SDL_DestroyWindow (SDL_video.c:4503, which WindowSDL's destructor
    reaches) restore the desktop mode. If the process dies without destroying the window the mode is the OS's to put back
    (CDS_FULLSCREEN is the temporary kind) [INFERENCE, not tried: it would flip this machine's display].
  * SDL sends SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_PIXEL_SIZE_CHANGED for each size change, WindowSDL turns it into OnActualSizeUpdate, the
    presenter resizes its swap chain (ResizeBuffers keeps the tearing flag): this is the path of a mode change at any
    time; the DPI/display-scale change that a mode below the desktop's brings (SDL: 100 %) goes through OnDpiChanged.

The guest vblank's display lock (0440) and a mode change [from reading graphics_system.cpp; not run]:
  * UpdateDisplayLock runs on every guest vblank: it takes the helper's new stamps, fits the line, recomputes k =
    round(guest period / display period) and (re)locks when k changes, unlocks after a stale display (no stamp for 4
    periods + 50 ms, at once) or 30 evaluations in a row of a rate that does not fit. Every 2 s it looks up the game window
    (FindGameWindow: the largest visible, non-minimized top-level window of the process) and its monitor, and restarts the
    helper when the monitor changed or the window is gone.
  * At start-up the window is already in its mode when the first lookup finds it, so the lock starts on the new rate: `display
    lock on: output 120.0xxx Hz ... every 2 of them` (k = 2 at 120 Hz) within about 3 s of the window opening. Mode at 60 Hz:
    k = 1. Alt-tab: the window is minimized, FindGameWindow finds none, the helper is stopped (`display lock off`, the QPC
    grid carries on), and the restored window is found at the next lookup (<= 2 s) and locked after >= 48 stamps.
  * If WaitForVBlank on the helper's IDXGIOutput stops working across the switch, `failed` is set, the lock is dropped and
    the lookup is retried after 5 s; if it keeps working, the fit follows (nine stamps in a row off the line restart it).
    A refresh that is no k x 60 Hz leaves the QPC grid (`display lock not used`), as before. Nothing in 0440 needs a change.

Checked (this machine: 3200x2000 panel, 120 Hz; nothing here switched its display mode):
  * clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only with the SDK's Release flags on window_sdl.cpp, window.cpp, d3d12_presenter.cpp: 0 errors,
    no new warnings; clang-format clean (the repo's .clang-format) on the touched files.
  * A harness that compiles the patch's ParseFullscreenMode and ChooseDisplayMode as they are against the SDK's SDL3
    (SDL_Init(VIDEO) only, enumeration only). The primary display lists 28 modes (14 sizes x 60 and 120 Hz, 24 bits,
    density 1; 3200x2000 down to 640x480, 1280x800, 1920x1200 and 1600x1000 among them). guest 1280x800 -> 1280x800@120;
    1920x1200 -> @120; 1280x800@60 -> 60; @144 -> 120 with the note; 1300x800 -> 1600x1000 with the note; 4000x3000 -> no
    mode (desktop + reason); parse: desktop, "", guest, GUEST@120, 1280x800, 1080p, 4k, "1280 x 800" accepted;
    desktop@120, 1280x, x800, guest@, @0, @5000, bogus refused.
  * Not run: the game, the mode switch itself, the presenter in the new mode.
Verify (Verifier, in a run with --fullscreen_mode=guest and a 1280x800 guest): the two lines above in the log, in this
order, then `[guest-vblank] display lock on ... every 2` and `src=display` in the 10 s lines; PresentMon PresentMode
"Hardware: Independent Flip" (not "Composed: Flip") with the allow-tearing flag; the desktop is back after alt-tab, after
a clean exit and after taskkill /F (scratch/S8/enum_modes.py prints the current mode on its first line); GPU busy
against the same run with fullscreen_mode=desktop. If tearing shows (on a fixed-refresh panel a Present(0, ALLOW_TEARING)
in independent flip flips at once, mid-scan-out [INFERENCE]), --d3d12_allow_variable_refresh_rate_and_tearing=false
presents without the flag.
